-> [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.flashing|Install OpenWrt (generic explanation)]]

The official web interface "Firmware Update" will refuse the OpenWrt image, so you have to flash the router via tftp:

  - Turn off the router
  - Press and hold the RESET button (one between the WAN and USB ports)
  - Turn on the router
  - Wait until the power LED begins to blink slowly, then release the RESET button (approx. 20-30 sec)
  - Connect your PC with one of the router's LAN ports
  - On your PC, configure static IP 192.168.1.2 netmask 255.255.255.0
  - Use atftp 192.168.1.1\\ <code>
tftp> mode octet
tftp> put openwrt-*.trx
tftp> quit
</code>
  - If the image received successfully, the power led will stop blinking
  - Wait several minutes until the router reboots and other LEDs come up (approx. 10 min)


